Note that yes, his _first_ 23 games are ascensions.  That does, indeed,
mean that he ascended 23 in a row without dying.  Watch his tactics and
learn from them--what he does _works_.  A key for me was realizing that
there are people out there who can ascend well over 50% of their
characters--that means that if you aren't doing so, it isn't the "cruel
RNG", it's poor play.  The game is beatable, the RNG isn't out to get
you, and pure strategy and good tactics can tilt the odds in your
favor.

Once you recognize that, you're well on the way to actually learning
good strategy and play for yourself.

Watch mrivan.  Watch rast, jove, eidolos, anselmus, etc.  See what they
do, emulate it, and win.

It took 10 years for my first ascension, and less than 1 year more to
be at the point where I could ascend over 10% of my games; things keep
improving.  It's been 5 for you.  Set your goal to learn something from
every game and not repeat the same mistake again.  And when you die,
don't just thing about what killed you then--try to consider if
something 10 levels back was a bad choice that got you stuck in the
final predicament.



